00:34:33,199 --> 00:34:35,739
and these here are all
non-negative numbers.

375
00:34:35,739 --> 00:34:38,746
This means that this number
here must be non-negative.

376
00:34:42,920 --> 00:34:47,320
If x is 0, then that's
where we want it.

377
00:34:47,320 --> 00:35:00,360
So we're done if f
of x0 is actually 0.

378
00:35:00,360 --> 00:35:09,000
So assume that f of x0 is
then strictly less than 0.

379
00:35:13,050 --> 00:35:19,730
But if the value here
is strictly less than 0,

380
00:35:19,730 --> 00:35:23,190
if this is the case,
then there exists--

381
00:35:23,190 --> 00:35:25,590
then if you take--

382
00:35:25,590 --> 00:35:32,690
so here, you have 0.

383
00:35:32,690 --> 00:35:35,250
Here, you have f of x0.

384
00:35:38,090 --> 00:35:40,870
You can then take a
little interval around it.

385
00:35:45,590 --> 00:36:04,110
So take epsilon bigger than
0 such that this thing here--

386
00:36:04,110 --> 00:36:10,530
such that f of x0 plus epsilon,
this is still negative.

387
00:36:18,950 --> 00:36:24,550
So I'm going to look at--
so here, I have f of x0.

